{
  "kanji": "格",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 格\ntitle: rank; character\njlpt: 3\ntags: [jlpt-n3, grade-5, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 10\nradical: 木\nradicalNumber: 75\nonyomi: [カク, コウ, キャク, ゴウ]\nkunyomi: []\ndistractors: [校, 杯, 果]\n---\n\n# 格 — rank; character\n\n**Strokes:** 10 · **Key (radical):** 木 (no. 75) · **JLPT:** N3 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n格 concerns rank, standing, or character. In [性格](../words/性格.md) (せいかく), it helps describe a person's personality.\nIn 資格 (しかく), the concern is qualifications, not whether someone has a pleasant personality.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** imagine a rank label in the small square at the bottom of the right-hand 各, attached beside 木.\nThis is a visual aid, not a proposed etymology.\n\n## Readings\n\nThe examples focus on カク; コウ, キャク, and ゴウ remain in the source metadata.\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| カク | on | [性格](../words/性格.md) せいかく — personality; 合格 ごうかく — passing an exam |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [性格](../words/性格.md) せいかく — personality; disposition\n- 合格 ごうかく — passing an examination; meeting a standard\n- 資格 しかく — qualifications; requirements\n\n## Notes\n\nIn ごうかく, ごう belongs to 合 and かく belongs to 格: do not infer a reading from the wrong half of a compound.\n[校](校.md) also has 木 on the left, but its right side is 交 rather than 各.\nEnglish \"character\" here means qualities or nature, not a written letter.\n",
